    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d923">

                <pb facs="1431" n="1417" sameAs="frus:frus1944v01/pg1417"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00110 E.W./9–444</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Soviet Ambassador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Gromyko</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Translation]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-09-04">September 4,
                        1944</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Secretary</hi>: The Soviet Government
                    has taken note of the memorandum sent to the Embassy on August 24, 1944, by the
                    Department of State,<anchor n="26" xml:id="d923-f1"/> and also of the enclosed
                    paraphrase of your telegram sent to the American Minister in Bern, in which you
                    give him instructions regarding the necessity of making representations to the
                    Swiss Government on the question of the non-admission into neutral countries of
                    the leaders of the Axis Powers and their adherents.</p>
                <p>I am happy to inform you that the Soviet Government shares the views of the
                    Government of the United States of America on this question.</p>
                <p>Sincerely yours,</p>
                <closer>[For the] Ambassador<lb/>[Signature illegible]</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
